stribution differently in BGP. The precise translation would depend on whether this is for LDP or BGP label distribution.\", 'trans_template': 'then tag mpls'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'then next-hop-self', 'parent_command': ['set policy-options policy-statement policy1 term 1 then accept'], 'root': 'set policy-options policy-statement policy1 term 1 then accept', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI `apply mpls-label` command:\\n\\n##\\nthen set forwarding-class mpls\\n##\\n\\nOr alternatively, if you specifically need the MPLS label application in route policy context:\\n\\n##\\nthen tag mpls\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact Juniper equivalent depends on the context. In Juniper:\\n1. `set forwarding-class mpls` is used for MPLS forwarding decisions\\n2. `tag mpls` can be used in routing policies to mark routes for MPLS handling\\n\\nFor BGP label distribution (which seems to be the context here), you might also consider:\\n##\\nthen next-hop-self\\n##\\nas Juniper handles label distribution differently in BGP. The precise translation would depend on whether this is for LDP or BGP label distribution.\", 'trans_template': 'then next-hop-self'}]]": 1,
